    description: "The district is line 6250 from Bergheim via Bf Neustadt to Talsee and the branch to Waldau, with the maintenance base at Bf Neustadt. A report says what is seen, not why: each fault has a cause drawn from what it can turn out to be, with the trade that can repair it (signalling, track, or any team) and the work it takes; the dispatcher sees how often it is which trade's, from experience. A team is of one trade. Sent to a fault, it drives there; where the work is in a track, it waits for the closure, which the dispatcher asks of the signaller (after 90 s the team asks itself); then it looks for the cause and reports it. What it does then is the dispatcher's word where there is more than one way: a team of the right trade repairs for good, or provisionally where the cause allows it (faster, but the repair may fail again within the shift: then the fault is back, with its cause known); a team of the other trade leaves, or stays to secure a danger until the right team comes (and repairs nothing meanwhile). A team sent into the track without a closure is a danger to people. A technician of each trade is on call: ready at the base after ten minutes, four hours of overtime. In a session the signaller's fault report arrives as a flow, the team's steps go back as the repair status (reported for a fault of the district's own report paths, then dispatched, arrived, diagnosed, working, done, secured, left, relapsed), the closure is asked of the signaller's game and comes back as a track closure; the staff plan sets the teams, the condition of the assets how many faults the shift brings. Alone, the game brings the signaller's fault itself and its own signallers close the tracks. The view has the district as a sketch: the places, the faults with the teams that can be sent, the teams at their places or on the road (a free team with the faults it can go to, one that secures a place to be called off), and the base, from which the technicians on call are called; a move that needs a second thing of the picture names it (target), so that the table (web/game/district.js), which shows both, can offer it there. The faults are those the table shows: at Bf Neustadt, and on the stretches of the district towards Bergheim, towards Talsee (the level crossing of Brückenstraße) and on the branch to Waldau. A track is closed by the signaller who reported the fault, or by the one named where somebody else reported it (closer).",
